{"path":"std/fs/index.html","title":"Module fs","description":"Filesystem manipulation operations.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Module fs"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#1-3484","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Filesystem manipulation operations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module contains basic methods to manipulate the contents of the local filesystem. All methods in this module represent cross-platform filesystem operations. Extra platform-specific functionality can be found in the extension traits of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"std::os::$platform"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"time-of-check-to-time-of-use-toctou","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time of Check to Time of Use (TOCTOU)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Many filesystem operations are subject to a race condition known as “Time of Check to Time of Use” (TOCTOU). This occurs when a program checks a condition (like file existence or permissions) and then uses the result of that check to make a decision, but the condition may have changed between the check and the use."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, checking if a file exists and then creating it if it doesn’t is vulnerable to TOCTOU - another process could create the file between your check and creation attempt."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Another example is with symbolic links: when removing a directory, if another process replaces the directory with a symbolic link between the check and the removal operation, the removal might affect the wrong location. This is why operations like "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.remove_dir_all.html","title":"fn std::fs::remove_dir_all","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"remove_dir_all"}]},{"type":"text","value":" need to use atomic operations to prevent such race conditions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To avoid TOCTOU issues:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be aware that metadata operations (like "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.metadata.html","title":"fn std::fs::metadata","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"metadata"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.symlink_metadata.html","title":"fn std::fs::symlink_metadata","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"symlink_metadata"}]},{"type":"text","value":") may be affected by changes made by other processes."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use atomic operations when possible (like "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html#method.create_new","title":"associated function std::fs::File::create_new","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"File::create_new"}]},{"type":"text","value":" instead of checking existence then creating)."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep file open for the duration of operations."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"structs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structs"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.DirBuilder.html","title":"struct std::fs::DirBuilder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DirBuilder"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A builder used to create directories in various manners."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.DirEntry.html","title":"struct std::fs::DirEntry","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DirEntry"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Entries returned by the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.ReadDir.html","title":"struct std::fs::ReadDir","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"ReadDir"}]},{"type":"text","value":" iterator."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html","title":"struct std::fs::File","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An object providing access to an open file on the filesystem."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.FileTimes.html","title":"struct std::fs::FileTimes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FileTimes"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Representation of the various timestamps on a file."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.FileType.html","title":"struct std::fs::FileType","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FileType"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A structure representing a type of file with accessors for each file type. It is returned by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.Metadata.html#method.file_type","title":"method std::fs::Metadata::file_type","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Metadata::file_type"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.Metadata.html","title":"struct std::fs::Metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Metadata"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Metadata information about a file."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.OpenOptions.html","title":"struct std::fs::OpenOptions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenOptions"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Options and flags which can be used to configure how a file is opened."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.Permissions.html","title":"struct std::fs::Permissions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Permissions"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Representation of the various permissions on a file."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.ReadDir.html","title":"struct std::fs::ReadDir","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ReadDir"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Iterator over the entries in a directory."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/struct.Dir.html","title":"struct std::fs::Dir","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dir"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An object providing access to a directory on the filesystem."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"enums","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Enums"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/enum.TryLockError.html","title":"enum std::fs::TryLockError","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TryLockError"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An enumeration of possible errors which can occur while trying to acquire a lock from the "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html#method.try_lock","title":"method std::fs::File::try_lock","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"try_lock"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method and "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html#method.try_lock_shared","title":"method std::fs::File::try_lock_shared","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"try_lock_shared"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method on a "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html","title":"struct std::fs::File","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"File"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Functions"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.canonicalize.html","title":"fn std::fs::canonicalize","children":[{"type":"text","value":"canonicalize"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the canonical, absolute form of a path with all intermediate components normalized and symbolic links resolved."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.copy.html","title":"fn std::fs::copy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"copy"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Copies the contents of one file to another. This function will also copy the permission bits of the original file to the destination file."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.create_dir.html","title":"fn std::fs::create_dir","children":[{"type":"text","value":"create_dir"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a new, empty directory at the provided path."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.create_dir_all.html","title":"fn std::fs::create_dir_all","children":[{"type":"text","value":"create_dir_all"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Recursively create a directory and all of its parent components if they are missing."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.exists.html","title":"fn std::fs::exists","children":[{"type":"text","value":"exists"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ok(true)"},{"type":"text","value":" if the path points at an existing entity."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.hard_link.html","title":"fn std::fs::hard_link","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hard_link"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a new hard link on the filesystem."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fs/fn.metadata.html","title":"fn std::fs::metadata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"metadata"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Given a path, queries th